  "articleBody": "Selecting the right floor plan service for your luxury property isn't as simple as just getting a drawing. You want a plan that accurately represents your home, whether it’s a waterfront estate in Key Biscayne or a penthouse in Sunny Isles Beach. Start by asking about their measurement standards – do they follow ANSI or another recognized standard? How do they calculate the area? You'll also want to confirm what's included: total area, room dimensions, wall thicknesses, and outdoor spaces are all crucial. Don't forget to inquire about their process, from how measurements are collected (laser tools and CAD drafting are good signs) to how revisions are handled. It's really important to match the accuracy and documentation to how you intend to use the plan. If square footage is commercially sensitive, for instance, you'll need a higher level of precision. Always clarify the stated tolerance – 'accurate' isn't enough; you want specifics.",
  "datePublished": "2026-10-01"
}